[def "Parameter name: [emph "datapolicyproc"]"]
Optional Tcl command prefix receiving a context dictionary after DATA is parsed and before message forwarding or dataproc. Contains id, phase data, peeraddr, sender, helo and recipients (after alias expansion). Returns action accept, defer or reject with optional reason/message, like recipientpolicyproc; trusted local clients bypass it. Use smtpd::policychain to accumulate findings and express combined policies: smtpd::spfpolicy collects SPF without rejecting, smtpd::dkimkeypolicy collects key diagnostics and sets dkim-no-key only when every provided signature key is definitively absent. Unsigned messages, lookup errors, invalid tags and signature-limit exhaustion do not set that finding; keys are not cryptographically verified. Configuring this hook buffers relay DATA up to maxdata before forwarding, preserving original wire bytes. Rejection returns 550 5.7.1 for the whole message; errors defer with 451. Decisions are logged as message-policy with accumulated findings. Empty preserves existing streaming behavior



